        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[url('/static/hero_images/singer.jpg')] bg-cover bg-center"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-white/80 via-white/70 to-[#FAFAFA] dark:from-[#0b1437]/90 dark:via-[#0b1437]/80 dark:to-[#0b1437]"></div>
        
        <div class="relative z-10 text-center px-6 mt-16">
            <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-7xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-4 tracking-tight drop-shadow-lg">Use Your Gifts.</h1>
            <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 font-medium max-w-2xl mx-auto drop-shadow-md">You were created on purpose, with purpose — now step into it.</p>
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Main Content Overlapping Hero -->
    <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full px-6 py-8 -mt-16 relative z-20 macos-glass mb-12">
        
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><span class="bg-gray-100 dark:bg-white/10 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider flex items-center gap-1"><svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 8v4l3 3m6-3a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg> 3 MIN READ</span></div><div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10 pb-6">
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">Serving</h2>
            <div class="w-24 h-1 rounded-full opacity-80" style="background-color: #eab308"></div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="prose  max-w-none">
            <div class="mb-8"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Created to Serve</h3><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Ephesians 2:10 says, "We are God's handiwork, created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which God prepared in advance for us to do." Let that sink in — before you ever took your first breath, God had already mapped out ways for you to make an impact in this world. You were not saved just to sit in a chair on Sunday and consume content. You were rescued, redeemed, and re-commissioned to make a real difference in the lives of people around you.</p></div><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">Every single believer has a role in the body of Christ. Paul makes this clear in 1 Corinthians 12:4-7 — there are different kinds of gifts, but the same Spirit distributes them for the common good. The church is not a spectator sport.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">It's a family on mission, and your participation matters more than you realize. When you serve, you step into the fullness of what God designed you for, and something comes alive inside you that sitting on the sidelines can never produce.</p></div><div class="mb-8"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Discover Your Gifts</h3><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">The Holy Spirit gives every believer spiritual gifts — not just pastors, not just "super Christians," but every person who has placed their trust in Jesus. Romans 12:6-8 lays out gifts like prophecy, serving, teaching, encouragement, generosity, leadership, and mercy. First Corinthians 12 expands the list even further.</p></div><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">The point isn't to find the "best" gift — it's to discover yours and use it faithfully.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Maybe you're the person who notices when someone is sitting alone and walks over to welcome them. Maybe you're the one who can organize chaos into clarity, or the one whose voice lifts an entire room into worship. Don't compare your gift to someone else's — contribute what you've been given.</p><div class="p-6 bg-gray-50 hover:bg-gray-100 dark:hover:bg-white/10 transition-all duration-300 transform hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg dark:bg-white/5 rounded-2xl border-l-4 my-6" style="border-color: currentColor"><p class="text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed italic">The body needs every part functioning (1 Corinthians 12:21-22). The eye can't say to the hand, "I don't need you." Your gift fills a gap that no one else can fill in exactly the same way.</p></div></div><div class="mb-8"><h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-3"><svg class="w-6 h-6 opacity-70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"></path></svg>Where You Can Serve</h3><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">We have real, tangible opportunities for you to jump in and make an impact right now. Our Worship Team needs vocalists, instrumentalists, and sound engineers who want to lead people into God's presence. Our Production & Media team handles cameras, graphics, live streaming, and social media — if you're creative or tech-savvy, this is your lane.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Our Hospitality team is the front door of our church: greeting, setup, teardown, and making sure every person who walks through the door feels seen and valued.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">Beyond Sunday, our Youth & Kids Ministry needs mentors and leaders who can invest in the next generation. Our Outreach & Evangelism teams take the gospel beyond our walls into the community through service projects, neighborhood initiatives, and relational evangelism. And our Prayer Team undergirds everything we do by interceding for our church, our city, and our world.</p><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">There is a place for you here — we promise. Whatever your skill set, your personality, or your season of life, God wants to use you right where you are.</p></div><div class="macos-card p-8 mb-8"><h4 class="font-bold text-xl mb-4 text-gray-900 dark:text-white">The First-Serve Experience</h4><p class="text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 text-lg">Not sure where you fit? That's completely okay — most people aren't when they start. That's why we created our low-pressure "Shadow" experience. You come alongside an existing team for one single gathering, watch how things work, ask all the questions you want, and get a real feel for what serving in that area looks like. There's zero commitment required — just a willingness to explore and see where the Holy Spirit might be leading you. Many of our most passionate team members started with a single Shadow Sunday and discovered a calling they never expected. Take the first step — God will meet you there.</p></div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-white/10">
            <a  href="/#join" class="w-full text-white font-bold text-lg py-5 rounded-xl hover:opacity-90 transition-all shadow-lg transform hover:-translate-y-1"  style="background-color: #eab308">
                Sign Up for a Shadow Sunday
            </a>
        </div>
    </main>
